{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CeGFDA2Prytk7v2Si4e6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Root Cause\n\nThe failure is **not** in `routes/public.map` — the map file is correct:\n\n```\n/health health\n/* wildcard\n```\n\nThe bug is in the Go source, `router/routes.go`:\n\n```go\npackage router\nfunc HealthHandler() string { return \"wildcard\" }\n```\n\n`HealthHandler()` is hardcoded to return `\"wildcard\"` instead of resolving/returning `\"health\"` (the value mapped to `/health` in `routes/public.map`). This effectively makes the health route behave as if it fell through to the `/*` wildcard entry, hence the test failure message `\"shadowed by wildcard\"`.\n\n**Fix location:** `router/routes.go` — `HealthHandler` needs to actually return `\"health\"` (i.e., look up/return the value associated with the `/health` route) rather than a hardcoded `\"wildcard\"` string. No changes to `routes/public.map` are needed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":3399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":501},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5bbf108f-4c05-4f08-abb4-d33a3d7f577d","uuid":"55a530e7-0d54-44be-ad01-cc9f07b9b7b4","timestamp":"2026-08-21T16:56:15.839Z","request_id":"req_011CeGFD9GkfvD2XE1MdZshY"}
